# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# The derivative of the energy in the charges with particle mesh Ewald
# (D[tunable-gradient-pme], docs/python-gradient.md) on the GPU, in double
# and mixed precision: 25 entries tied by a map on the dipeptide in water
# with a net charge, the direct sum, the potential of the grid at the
# particles, the self term, the background, and the excluded and 1-4 pairs
# against central differences of the energy; and the same in a triclinic
# cell, 403 waters in a rhombic dodecahedron.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_gradient.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide pme GPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_gradient.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide pme GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the charges with particle mesh Ewald, 25 entries for 1168 particles, a net charge of 0.5 e, against central differences of the energy
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: in a triclinic cell, 11 entries for 1209 particles, against central differences of the energy
# CHECK: pme passed
